        "text": "Memory Segments\nToo much stuff, right? Don\u2019t worry; you will quickly understand reverse engi-\nneering if you grasp the basics of assembly language first.\nIn Figure 15.5, you can see the memory segmentation areas. The text area is\nwhere the assembly instructions are stored. The data and BSS are for variable\nstorage. The heap is a location at the memory where you can store and manip-\nulate data dynamically. Finally, the famous stack is managed by the compiler.",
